Nope; I never recall having to deal with Jacobians in MCSim.

In most (all?) commercial system dynamics simulators, one specifies the
time step for the simulation.  Then one has to test if it's short enough
(and not too short), and sometimes one forgets to test after changing
the model.  MCSim made that automatic, while still letting one choose to
set it manually.

>> - that something about MCSim led me naturally to designed experiments instead of OFAT experiments on models from the very beginning
>
