An Akima interpolator, unlike some others, allows unequal spacing of the
independent variable and is, I think, better behaved than a polynomial
interpolator.  I don't really want to have to specify (x,y) points for
x=1:100 if nothing interesting happens to y between x=20 and x=80, for
example.

