                           real beta,
                           real<lower=0> sigma) {
       alpha ~ cauchy(0,2.5);
       beta ~ cauchy(0,2.5);
       sigma ~ cauchy(0,5);
       for (n in 1:N)
         y[n] ~ normal(alpha * x[n] + beta, sigma);
   }

linear_regression() is the function we're defining.  I think the
ode is going to produce a function that's defined with respect
to some parameters (e.g., the rate parameters and saturation parameters
