That's fair.  A system dynamicist might view it as more of a state
variable problem (or even analog computer problem): the set of
integrator outputs defines the state of the system.  We refer to those
as the stocks or levels in the system.  The derivatives (flows into or
out of a stock) we call flows or rates (to match the stocks or levels
terminology).

