Just quickly:  I agree with Mike that we should forget about trying to solve muliple modes.  If we get lucky and can handle a problem with multiple modes, fine, but that can't be our plan.
But we have lots of non-multimodal problems with slow mixing, including various stan-users queries recently. Even the 8 schools has problems if it's not Matt-tricked.  And we do want to be able to diagnose those.  And, in the short and medium term, we need some plan/recommendation of what to do when we have several chains and one or more are slow moving.  Maybe some way to hold the hand of HMC/Nuts to see if it can be pulled toward an area of faster motion?
A

