>
> I think we've had lots of success in the past few days with the usual suggestions -- think of your model more deeply and consider either better initialization (yes, this can potentially lead to bias so it's not perfect) and better priors that clean up the tail behavior.  To channel Andrew, "Folk theorem folk theorem folk theorem."  ;-)
