Most of these issues seem to be problems with adaptation being too aggressive in the tails.  Sharing adaptation information between chains (as we have discussed before) would help, but also require a significant amount of refactoring our code (we'd basically have to implement ensemble samplers).  Using SoftAbs is another option but, as previous discussed, will have to wait for the higher-order autodiff.

The easiest stopgap would be tweaked warmup -- I'll try to get to it by the end of the week.

