I think it's more important right now to get the
command-line stuff working for 2.0.   I'm getting really
antsy not having a release candidate that we trust.

I would rather put off making changes to adaptation or
other parts of the algorithms until we have a stable
2.0 version passing all tests.   For a start, all of these
issues are w.r.t. 1.3.  One advantage of 2.0, if I understand
